#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1119 expect=noViolation domain=CO
#note "FRESH, DISCRIMINATING. None of the thirteen Permissible Identifier/Timing columns (COGRPID, COREFID, COSPID, VISIT, VISITNUM, VISITDY, TAETORD, CODY, COTPT, COTPTNUM, COELTM, COTPTREF, CORFTDTC) is declared. The second conjunct is TRUE (RDOMAIN populated) so the whole first parenthesised disjunction must be FALSE. Predicted SILENT: each leaf is a POSITIVE not empty(X) over an absent column, which EC-43 folds to all-missing, and the derivation added no var_exists conjunct anywhere in this rule (the shipped expression is byte-identical to the authored one) precisely because none of those leaves flips on absence. All thirteen are Permissible in CO, so this dataset shape is fully conformant and must not be double-reported. If it fires, thirteen absent columns are being read as populated — escalate, do not rewrite."
#expectViolationCount 0
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset CO class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Comments"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col RDOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col COSEQ    type=Num
col IDVAR    type=Char
col IDVARVAL type=Char
col COVAL    type=Char
---
S1 | CO | AE | 001 | 1 | AESEQ | 1 | Comment on AE record
